            {
              "id": "e1ae6064-ebac-38b2-99de-bd8b8e0969e8",
              "name": "Potential Missing Function Level Access Control. View function lacks authentication/authorization decorators.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nFunction-level access control is missing. In this Python aiohttp view, the handler returns HTML content without first verifying that the caller is authenticated and allowed to access the route.\n\nA view function like `_root_view(request)` can be reached directly unless the application enforces authorization before rendering the response. If this endpoint is intended for authenticated users or a limited role, an unauthenticated or low-privilege caller may be able to retrieve protected content simply by requesting the URL.\n\nThe fix is to enforce both authentication and authorization at the start of the handler, before loading the template or returning any data. In aiohttp applications, this is commonly done by checking a user object placed on the request by authentication middleware and rejecting requests that lack the required role or permission.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nProtect every route that serves non-public content with a server-side authorization check. Do not rely on hidden links, client-side logic, or template names to restrict access. Ensure authentication middleware runs before the handler and stores the current principal on the request in a consistent location.\n\nUse deny-by-default rules and require explicit roles or permissions for sensitive endpoints. Return 401 for unauthenticated requests and 403 for authenticated users who lack permission. Centralize authorization in decorators or middleware so new handlers do not accidentally bypass access control, and add tests that verify anonymous and low-privilege users cannot access the route.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\n~~~python\nfrom aiohttp import web\nfrom aiohttp_jinja2 import get_template\n\n\ndef require_role(role_name):\n    def decorator(handler):\n        async def wrapped(request):\n            user = request.get(\"user\")\n            if user is None:\n                raise web.HTTPUnauthorized(text=\"Authentication required\")\n\n            roles = user.get(\"roles\", [])\n            if role_name not in roles:\n                raise web.HTTPForbidden(text=\"Insufficient permissions\")\n\n            return await handler(request)\n        return wrapped\n    return decorator\n\n\n@require_role(\"admin\")\nasync def _root_view(request):\n    template = get_template(\"index.html\", request.app)\n    html = template.render()\n    return web.Response(text=html, content_type=\"text/html\")\n~~~\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\n~~~python\naiohttp\naiohttp-jinja2\njinja2\n~~~\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Broken Access Control](https://owasp.org/www-community/Broken_Access_Control)\n- [OWASP Authorization Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Authorization_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-285: Improper Authorization](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html)\n- [aiohttp Web Server Quickstart](https://docs.aiohttp.org/en/stable/web_quickstart.html)\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-285",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/285.html"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "CWE-285"
                ]
              }
